    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eq-site-links",
      "x": 3470,
      "y": 2355,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 370,
      "text": "Earthquakes/index.html (Hub)\nTopics: Tectonic plates, seismology,\nAustralian context, Newcastle 1989\n\nMechanics_of_Earthquakes/index.html\n  Elastic rebound, seismic waves,\n  measurement scales\n\nPlate_Tectonics/index.html\n  Plate boundaries, subduction, Indo-\n  Australian Plate movement (7 cm/yr)\n\nFault_Types/index.html\n  Normal, reverse, strike-slip;\n  earthquake classification\n\nAustralian_Seismicity/index.html\n  Intraplate earthquakes, hidden faults,\n  55,000 quakes in 50 years\n\nSecondary_Hazards/index.html\n  Liquefaction, tsunamis, landslides,\n  firestorms",
